\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Distribution of optimal decoding strategies across the four datasets. Sampling decoding is optimal for 80-92\% of prompts across all datasets, explaining why routing provides no benefit when evaluated on individual datasets. Error bars show 95\% confidence intervals from 5-fold cross-validation.}}{6}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:fig2}{{2}{6}{Distribution of optimal decoding strategies across the four datasets. Sampling decoding is optimal for 80-92\% of prompts across all datasets, explaining why routing provides no benefit when evaluated on individual datasets. Error bars show 95\% confidence intervals from 5-fold cross-validation}{figure.2}{}}
